  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 Primary Election (June 2, 2026) - Elections - Cedar County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Skip to content\n \n\n \n\n Cedar County, Iowa\n Elections\n \n \n\n \n\n \n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections 2026 Primary Election\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \n2018 \n2017 \n2016 \n2015 \n2014 \n2013 \n2012 \n2011 \n2010 \n2009 \n2008 \n2007 \n2006 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n\n \n \n\n \n2026 Primary Election\n\n \nJune 2, 2026\n Primary Election \n \n\n The Primary Election is an election to determine which candidates will qualify for the General Election for a given party. In Iowa you must be a member of the political party of which you wish to vote for in order to participate. This is known as a \"closed primary.\" The primary election is held on the 1st Tuesday following the 1st Monday in June of each even-numbered year. \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n Results By Precinct · Unofficial\n \n \n\n All Precincts Counted \n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n Results Summary · Unofficial\n \n \n\n All Precincts Counted \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \nArchived Election Details\n \nCOUNTY CANDIDATE LIST AS OF 3.23.26 \n \n\n  \n \n\n  \n \n\n  \n \n\nVoter Registration \n \n \n \nVoter Pre-Registration deadline: Monday, May 18, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. \n \nVoters can register after May 18, 2026 by following the election day registration procedures (provide proof of identification (i.e. current and valid photo identification card with an expiration date) AND proof of residency in their voting precinct) when they go to the polls on election day, or when they request an absentee ballot in-person.  \n \n \n\nAbsentee Ballots \n \n\n     By Mail: \n \n \n \nRequest period for mailed Absentee Ballots: Tuesday, March 24, 2026 - Monday, May 18, 2026 \n \nAbsentee Ballot Request Form \n \nAbsentee Ballot request forms must be recieved by 5:00 p.m. on the deadline (postmarks do not count) \n \nElection Office Mailing Period for Absentee Ballots: Wednesday, May 13, 2026 - Monday, May 18, 2026 \n \nAll absentee ballots must be received at the Auditor's Office by 8:00 p.m. on Election Day to be considered on time to be counted. (postmarks do not count) \n \n \n\n     In-Person: \n \n \n \nAny Cedar County registered voters can vote In-Person Absentee during these times: \n \n \nRegular Voting Hours at the Auditor's Office: \n \n \n \nWednesday, May 13, 2026 - Monday, June 1, 2026 \n \nRegular Business Hours: M-F 8:00am - 4:00pm \n \n \n \nThe Auditor's Office will be close on Monday, May 25, 2026 in observance of Memorial Day \n \nExtended Voting Hours at the Auditor's Office: \n \n \nMonday, May 18, 2026 \n \n \n8:00am - 5:00pm \n \n \n \nFriday, May 29, 2026 \n \n \n8:00am - 5:00pm \n \n \n \nSaturday, May 30, 2026 \n \n \n7:00am - 3:00pm \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nElection Day Voting \n \n \n \nTUESDAY, JUNE 2, 2026 \n \nVOTE AT REGULAR POLLING LOCATIONS \n \nPOLLS WILL BE OPEN FROM 7:00 A.M. TO 8:00 p.m. \n \n \n\nAfter Election \n \n \n \nONLY CEDAR COUNTY UNOFFICIAL RESULTS ARE POSTED ON OUR WEBSITE. FOR RACES THAT ARE SHARED WITH OTHER COUNTIES PLEASE REFER TO THE STATEWIDE WEBSITE FOR GRAND TOTALS. \n \nCanvass of Votes: Tuesday, June, 9, 2026 \n \nRecount Request Deadline: Friday, June 12, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. \n \n \n\nCandidates  \n \n \n \nCandidate Filing Period: Monday, March 2, 2026 - Friday, March 20, 2026 at 5:00 p.m. \n \n \n \nCounty Positions up for election \n \n \n \nBoard of Supervisor (2) \n \nTreasurer \n \nAttorney \n \nRecorder \n \n \n \n \n \nCandidate Guide \n \nAffidavit of Candidacy \n \nNomination Petition \n \n \n\nElection Documents: \n \n\nPolling Locations \n \n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n Search\n \n \n \n\n Republican\n \n \n \n\n Democratic\n \n \n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n Cedar County Auditor\n\n Cedar County Courthouse\n \n400 Cedar Street\n \nTipton, IA 52772\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00AM to 4:00PM\n \nMonday - Friday \n \nPhone Numbers\n\n Office: (563) 886-3168\n \nFax: (563) 866-3339 \n \n\n \n\n Contact Cedar County Elections\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
